{"title":"Career Roadmap · Design Engineer (R&D)","role":"Design Engineer (R&D)","summary":"A Design Engineer (R&D) converts product requirements into technically feasible, manufacturable, testable and reliable engineering designs.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Tech / B.E. (Bachelor of Technology / Engineering)","Course":"Design Engineering / Engineering Design"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"A Design Engineer (R&D) converts product requirements into technically feasible, manufacturable, testable and reliable engineering designs."},{"type":"p","text":"Depending on the industry, the engineer may design:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Mechanical components"},{"text":"Machines"},{"text":"Automotive systems"},{"text":"Industrial equipment"},{"text":"Consumer products"},{"text":"Robotics"},{"text":"Aerospace structures"},{"text":"Electronics enclosures"},{"text":"Mechatronic systems"},{"text":"Manufacturing equipment"},{"text":"Energy systems"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The role combines:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Engineering fundamentals","CAD","Product Design","Materials","Manufacturing","Simulation","Prototyping","Testing","Design for Manufacturing","R&D"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"The strongest profile is not merely someone who can create CAD models. It is someone who can take a product from:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Requirement","Concept","Engineering Design","Simulation","Prototype","Testing","Iteration","Manufacturing"]},{"type":"h","text":"Career Flow"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Tech/B.E. Design Engineering","Engineering Fundamentals","Design Thinking + Requirements","Concept Generation","Engineering Calculations","CAD Modeling","Material Selection","Manufacturing Process Selection","CAE / Simulation","Prototype Development","Testing & Validation","Design Iteration","DFM / DFA / Cost Optimization","Design Engineer — R&D","Senior Desi